+/* 2026-07-31 Move-panel bottom-clipping fix (see panels/move.py for the full
+ * measurement). The panel needed 226px of a 212px content area on this
+ * 320x240 kiosk, so GTK pushed the distance selector partly off the bottom
+ * edge. The row-homogeneity fixes in move.py close that deficit on their own;
+ * this rule just trims base.css's per-button margin .2em + padding .25em
+ * chrome for that panel to buy a little real headroom rather than landing
+ * exactly on the limit. Worth ~2px per jog button and ~4px per position
+ * readout -- small, but free. Scoped to an explicit class so no other panel's
+ * button metrics change, and chosen over ellipsizing or shrinking text so
+ * every label (notably the two-line "Disable Motors") stays full-size. */
+.move_compact {
+    margin: .05em;
+    padding: .05em;
+}
 
